do Resolve the absolute project and current user and repository branch
    conventions, including required prefixes. Return an object with project,
    naming_rules, current_branch, and start_ref set to the explicit parent
    branch or null. Never infer a parent from a PR target. as @context

do Read branch, HEAD, porcelain status, and active Git operation state together
    from @context.project. Return an object with attached_head, conflicts,
    active_operation, and current_branch. as @git_state

do Verify @git_state has an attached HEAD, no unresolved conflicts, and no
    active merge, rebase, cherry-pick, or revert.

do Use the supplied name or derive a concise task branch name under
    @context.naming_rules. When repository rules do not override it, use
    <type>/<TICKET-ID>-<lowercase-kebab-description> with the exact uppercase
    active ticket, type feature/bugfix/hotfix/chore/refactor/perf/test/release,
    and 1–6 lowercase letter or digit description words. Count description
    words only. Map Bug to bugfix and Story or new capability to feature. Reuse
    only the active ticket ID, type, and summary from conversation context when needed. Return an
    object with name, naming_ready, and missing_facts. as @naming

if @naming.naming_ready == false
    ask "Provide the missing branch name or task facts:" as @naming_input

    do Complete @naming from @naming_input under @context.naming_rules. Return
        an updated object with name, naming_ready, and missing_facts. as @naming

if @naming.naming_ready != true
    return "Branch creation stopped because the branch name is incomplete."

do Choose @context.start_ref when non-null, otherwise @git_state.current_branch.
    Verify it is an existing local branch with a configured upstream. Preserve
    uncommitted changes and do not stash, reset, or discard them. Return the
    branch name. as @parent_branch

run git -C @context.project switch @parent_branch as @switch_result

run git -C @context.project -c merge.autoStash=false -c rebase.autoStash=false pull --ff-only as @pull_result

do Compare @naming.name with local branches and known remote-tracking branches
    without fetching. Return true when the name already exists, otherwise false. as @branch_exists

if @branch_exists == true
    do Choose the first unused suffix -2, -3, and so on for @naming.name.
        Preserve required prefix and ticket, shortening the description only
        when needed to retain naming limits. Never reuse or reset an existing
        task branch. Return the updated naming object. as @naming

do Verify @naming.name is unused, follows @context.naming_rules, and any supplied
    ticket matches the active ticket. Do not use a converter or a generated validator.

run git -C @context.project switch -c @naming.name as @creation

print Report @naming.name and @creation briefly without reinspection.
